node_modules/
dist/
rust/target/
# Cargo also writes a target dir for the packages that are not the server: the
# WASM client builds into `web/client/target/`, and a direct `cargo test` on a
# shared crate writes `crates/<name>/target/`. Neither is under `rust/`, so they
# need their own lines. `dist/` above has no slash, so it already covers
# `server/dist/`.
crates/*/target/
web/client/target/
/public/
data/
storage/
.env
*.log
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
